      "report_date": "2026-11-06",
      "title": "Threat actors use agentic AI tooling to find and abuse exposed secrets",
      "summary": "Microsoft observed threat actors using ARTEX, an agentic AI offensive framework, to scan public GitHub repositories for exposed credentials, application secrets, and AI inference API keys. The agents analyze scan results and carry out follow-on attacks, reducing the need for hands-on operator involvement. In one case, an AI agent moved from searching GitHub for secrets to exfiltrating data from Azure Key Vault in five minutes. Activity beginning October 28, 2026 used compromised service principal credentials to access Entra ID tenants, Azure resources, and Microsoft 365 data across multiple organizations. Microsoft advises rotating exposed secrets immediately, since removing them from code does not revoke them, and migrating OAuth apps to managed identities.",
      "completeness": "Medium",
