      "report_date": "2026-11-06",
      "title": "A signed “Abe Office” helper that opens your browser behind your back",
      "summary": "AbeAgent.exe is a modular remote-access trojan that presents itself as an \"Abe Office\" helper and is signed with a certificate in the name of an individual, with no real Abe Office product behind it. Its starter program unlocks three encrypted add-ons after contacting its server, but the unlock key can be derived from a default password left in the file, so the add-ons and traffic could be fully decrypted. The add-ons give the operator a hidden desktop that reuses the victim's copied Chrome and Edge profiles, plus a browser stealer that bypasses App-Bound Encryption. In a multi-day sandbox run, the operator opened hidden browsers and went straight to saved-password pages. Defenders should watch for the AbeOffice folders, the Run value, and outbound traffic to the listed C2 servers on port 9090.",
